{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DoF1EBh3EZJar7Nso7Vozd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DFT binding energy atomic oxygen Cu(111) fcc hollow eV relative to gas-phase O atom PW91 PBE\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CO adsorption on Cu(111) and Cu(001) surfaces: improving site preference in DFT calculations\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0408394\"},{\"title\":\"Non-adiabatic Effects in the Dissociation of Oxygen Molecules at the Al(111) Surface\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/0704.2202\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2505.12914\"},{\"title\":\"s11433 012 4868 5\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s11433-012-4868-5.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Structural and electronic properties of atomic oxygen adsorption on Cu(111) surface: A first-principles investigation\",\"url\":\"https://bvbvf1.bib-bvb.de/vufind/PrimoRecord/cdi_chongqing_primary_44769476\"},{\"title\":\"CO adsorption on Cu(111) and Cu(001) surfaces: improving site preference in DFT calculations\",\"url\":\"https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/cond-mat/0408394\"},{\"title\":\"skip to main content\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/pages/biblio/1440993-atomic-molecular-adsorption-cu\"},{\"title\":\"August 19, 2004\",\"url\":\"https://www.pnnl.gov/publications/effect-sn-reactivity-cu-surfaces\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0511679v2\"},{\"title\":\"First principles study of oxidation resistance of atomically flat Cu(111) surface\",\"url\":\"https://https-meetings--archive-aps-org-443.webvpn1.xju.edu.cn/mar/2022/g47/5/\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a direct PW91-versus-PBE comparison for atomic O on Cu(111) referenced to a gas-phase O atom, but it did surface a few relevant values.\n\n- **PBE, fcc hollow:** One PBE study reports a binding energy of -5.000 eV for O on the fcc site, with the hcp site at -4.905 eV (Oxygen (O*) fcc -5.000; hcp -4.905). The same paper says its energies are referenced to an isolated gas-phase oxygen atom (EX is the energy of an isolated oxygen atom in the gas phase). The snippet doesn't show the full reference formula, so I can't confirm the sign convention from it.\n- **Site preference:** Several studies agree that the threefold hollow sites are favored. One reports that the fcc-hollow site is the most stable site for oxygen adsorption, and another finds that the coverage-dependent adsorption energy weakens as oxygen coverage rises (The adsorption energy decreases with increasing oxygen coverage due to the increasing repulsive interaction in the overlayer O adatoms.).\n- **PW91:** A PNNL study compared PW91 and RPBE for atomic O on Cu(111), but the snippet doesn't include its numbers, so I can't give a PW91 value for this system.\n- **Related PW91 data:** For CO on Cu(111) at 1/4 ML, PW91 gives fcc-hollow adsorption energies of about -0.84 eV, with RPBE values in brackets (-0.84[-0.46](-0.27)). This is a different adsorbate, so it's only a rough methodological reference.\n\nTo get a clean PW91 and PBE pair for atomic O, referenced to the gas-phase atom, the PNNL paper or the original Cu(111) O adsorption studies would be the next places to check.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72fc6f35-890f-436c-848d-a577c82337fb","uuid":"e11f20f2-83df-4e93-9580-56b71d61c188","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:09:02.584Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"DFT binding energy atomic oxygen Cu(111) fcc hollow eV relative to gas-phase O atom PW91 PBE","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_016PGxaVSEbZBRzaTAJ3vgnw","content":[{"title":"CO adsorption on Cu(111) and Cu(001) surfaces: improving site preference in DFT calculations","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0408394"},{"title":"Non-adiabatic Effects in the Dissociation of Oxygen Molecules at the Al(111) Surface","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/0704.2202"